{"draft": true, "session": {"id": "41be4838-da9b-42fc-a326-1b8f0b4ecdec", "startedAt": "2026-08-27T16:14:33.559Z", "endedAt": "2026-08-27T16:38:07.401Z", "firstUserMessage": "your task is to rethink the config generation that the backend does, to make animations for tracks.\n- have a think about what to sidechain to what\n  - e.g. the human eye can notice shape movement easier than colour changes, so only modulate colour as a transition, or slowly, and modulate fractal shape via vocals/bass.\n  - create variation that matches the track and breaks up repetition, e.g. modulate x & y offset by width, stems for first 16 bars of drop, then switch some things up for the next 16, and maybe switch one sidechain to kick or snare for the last 16 until the mid section\n  - transition to new shapes and colours at drops/mid-sections\n  - \"float\" during floaty sections\n  - avoid at all costs - flickering or sudden jumps\n  - use a mix of bezier curves, patterns and sidechains\n  - the fractal should always be visible (i.e. not a black screen)\n  - the animation frame should not be filled with block colour, this is too bright, and people can't actually see anything\n  - the fractal should always look aesthetic.\n\nas an exercise, make a series of \"voting\" scenarios/demos/questions that I can use to steer the direction (see the one we did a couple of hours ago)", "totals": {"diff": {"added": 1, "removed": 2, "files": 5}, "tokens": {"in": 3458, "out": 75493, "cacheRead": 3928866, "cacheCreate": 572024}}}, "totals": {"diff": {"added": 1, "removed": 2, "files": 5}, "tokens": {"in": 3458, "out": 75493, "cacheRead": 3928866, "cacheCreate": 572024}}, "eyebrow": "session 41be4838", "title": "your task is to rethink the config generation that the backend does, to make animations f…", "subtitle": "", "footer": "", "respawnOf": null, "groups": [], "extraStats": [], "agents": [{"id": "41be4838-da9b-42fc-a326-1b8f0b4ecdec:main", "parent": null, "type": "main", "model": null, "title": "you